qca-ssdk: match the kernel's .match_phy_device prototype

cmcc,pz-l8 needs IN_MP_PHY=TRUE for the IPQ5018 internal GE PHY, and
src/hsl/phy/mpge_phy.c / mpge_led.c call qca808x_phy_set_wol_status(),
qca808x_phy_get_eee_cap() and qca808x_phy_led_ctrl_source_set() directly.
IN_MP_PHY therefore implies IN_QCA808X_PHY (ssdk's own config sets both for
CHIP_TYPE=MP), which builds src/hsl/phy/qca808x.c - and that still uses the
single-argument .match_phy_device prototype.

Upstream changed the op to take the candidate phy_driver in v6.16, and
OpenWrt backports it into 6.12 (generic/backport-6.12/782-01-v6.16-net-phy-
pass-PHY-driver-to-.match_phy_device-OP.patch), so LINUX_VERSION_CODE cannot
distinguish the two.  The package Makefile greps include/linux/phy.h and
defines SSDK_MATCH_PHY_DEVICE_HAS_DRV accordingly.

The body is unchanged: it only looks at phydev->phy_id and phydev->drv,
whose meaning during matching is the same under both prototypes.

--- a/src/hsl/phy/qca808x.c
+++ b/src/hsl/phy/qca808x.c
@@ -600,7 +600,19 @@
 	return err;
 }
 
+/*
+ * OpenWrt backports upstream v6.16's two-argument .match_phy_device into
+ * kernel 6.12 (generic/backport-6.12/782-01-v6.16-net-phy-pass-PHY-driver-
+ * to-.match_phy_device-OP.patch), so LINUX_VERSION_CODE cannot tell the two
+ * prototypes apart.  The package Makefile greps include/linux/phy.h and
+ * defines SSDK_MATCH_PHY_DEVICE_HAS_DRV when the tree has the new form.
+ */
+#ifdef SSDK_MATCH_PHY_DEVICE_HAS_DRV
+int qca808x_match_phy_device(struct phy_device *phydev,
+			     const struct phy_driver *phydrv)
+#else
 int qca808x_match_phy_device(struct phy_device *phydev)
+#endif
 {
 	a_uint32_t phy_id = 0;
 
